@startuml
title Vapor Operational State Model

hide empty description

state "Steam App Instance Situation" as Situation {

    state "Capability" as Capability {
        [*] --> Player
        Player --> Composer : upgrade
        Composer --> Player : downgrade

        Composer --> ContentDeveloper : upgrade
        ContentDeveloper --> Composer : downgrade

        ContentDeveloper --> EcosystemDeveloper : upgrade
        EcosystemDeveloper --> ContentDeveloper : downgrade

        EcosystemDeveloper --> RootAuthority : root authority
    }

    --

    state "Composition Resolution" as Resolution {
        [*] --> Unresolved
        Unresolved --> Resolved : resolve succeeds
        Unresolved --> Invalid : resolve fails

        Resolved --> Unresolved : relevant source changes
        Invalid --> Unresolved : source/config changes
    }

    --

    state "Build Currency" as Build {
        [*] --> Missing

        Missing --> Building : build
        Stale --> Building : rebuild
        Failed --> Building : retry

        Building --> Current : success
        Building --> Failed : failure

        Current --> Stale : relevant source/composition change
    }

    --

    state "Local Vapor App" as Installation {
        [*] --> NotInstalled

        NotInstalled --> Installing : install / deploy
        Installing --> Installed : success
        Installing --> NotInstalled : failure

        Installed --> NotInstalled : remove
    }

    --

    state "Runtime" as Runtime {
        [*] --> Stopped

        Stopped --> Starting : launch
        Starting --> Running : start succeeds
        Starting --> Stopped : start fails

        Running --> Stopping : stop / exit
        Stopping --> Stopped : stopped
        Running --> Stopped : crash / abnormal exit
    }
}

note right of Situation
This is a projection of several
orthogonal state dimensions.

A real Vapor Situation is their
combination plus additional
conditions such as source state,
authentication, provider
availability, selection,
publication state, and tooling.

The model deliberately does not
enumerate every cross-product
as one giant serialized state machine.
end note

note bottom of Build
A failed rebuild does not
automatically destroy an older
installed working Vapor App.
end note

note bottom of Capability
Capability and remote
authorization are separate.
end note

@enduml